{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1359737-silent-reef-style-wip","id":1359737,"title":"Silent Reef Style (WIP)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-08T09:33:30-08:00","id":1359737,"title":"Silent Reef Style (WIP)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I dusted off one of my old martial arts styles and attempted to redesign it for 3rd Edition. At the moment, this is crude first draft and a first attempt at <i>any</i> 3rd Edition mechanics. So any critiques, suggestions, and other commentary are welcome. In particular, proper costs are eluding me. I don't have a good feel for how to value various effects yet, so any opinions on that front would be helpful.<br /> <br /> By way of a short introduction, this style was designed for a society of bounty hunting retiarii in the West. Once governed by a strict code, they've become increasingly fractured, with several renegade members engaging in more unscrupulous methods to apprehend their prey. Among traditionalists, it is preferred to bring their targets in alive.<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Reef Weapons:</b> Silent Reef style is rarely practiced unarmed, but its barehanded strikes are strong-armed grapples and strangling choke holds. Preferentially, the Silent Reef fights with the armaments of the fisherman - the net and the trident. The net is used to distract and unbalance as well as to bind, while the trident finds use when grim necessity demands a wounding blow.<br /> <br /> <b>Armor: </b>Silent Reef style is compatible with light armor.<br /> <br /> NEW WEAPON: TRIDENT<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Heavy (Accuracy +0, Damage +11, Defense -1, Overwhelming 1)<br /> Tags: Lethal, Melee, Disarming, Reaching, Two-Handed<br /> <br /> Note: If I were keeping true to 2nd Edition rules, this weapon would also have the Piercing tag. At the moment, I dropped it, thinking that might be too many tags for one weapon.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> NEW WEAPON: NET<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Medium (Damage +9, Overwhelming 1)<br /> Accuracy: Close +4; Short +3; Medium +2; Long -1; Extreme -3<br /> Tags: Thrown (Short), Grappling, Special<br /> <br /> Nets are often cast on lines, allowing the angler to more easily retrieve his catch. Once thrown, a net with such as casting line can be retrieved with a ready weapon action instead of moving to reclaim it. Nets do not inflict bashing or lethal damage, and therefore cannot normally be used as part of a decisive attack. They can be used to perform a grapple gambit out to their maximum range, usually employing Thrown as the relevant combat ability. Once the control roll has been made, the caster need not be involved with the grapple. If so, the victim suffers only the base effects of the grapple. If the caster wishes to make a savage, restrain/drag, or slam/throw action, they must be an active participate in the clinch, though they may stunt this through a casting line.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Fisher of Men Stance</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cost</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">: 3m;</span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 2, Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Dual</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The martial artist adopts the stance of the prepared angler, ready to strike with net or trident. The martial artist may reflexively perform a ready weapon action before her attack. If she attacks a target she successfully attacked with a different weapon on her last turn or more recently, her </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">withering</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> attack gains (higher of Essence or 3) bonus dice. If she performs a disarm or grapple gambit, her </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">decisive</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> attack doubles 9s.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The Clownfish Smiles</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 4m, 1i, 1wp; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Mastery, Perilous, Terrestrial, Uniform</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">As the clownfish is safe among the stinging arms of the anemone, the martial artist is safe within the grasp of his foes. When the martial artist is targeted by an attack while they are grappling with another enemy, she gains +2 Defense. If the attack misses the martial artist, her grappling opponent must defend against its rolled successes as though he were the original target, passing the onslaught penalty along as well. This Charm may be used once per grapple and resets once the current grapple ends.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mastery: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">If the martial artist controls the grapple and redirects an attack with this Charm, she regains 1 willpower.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Terrestrial:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The martial artist must control the grapple to use this Charm.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Entangled Krait Courtship</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 6m; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Decisive-Only, Mastery</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Fisher of Men Stance</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The sea krait entwines its mate, and the two snakes cannot be parted. The martial artist binds her foe in similarly inescapable embrace. This charm supplements a control roll during a grapple, doubling her 9s. Each 1 her opponent rolls subtracts one from his successes. If the martial artist wins control, she may not savage, slam or throw her target so long as she maintains the clinch. Restraining and dragging expend only 1 round of control.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mastery: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Restraining and dragging expend no rounds of control.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Polyp Proximity Strike</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 5m; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 3, Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Decisive-Only, Mastery</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: The Clownfish Smiles</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The reef is a massive predator, but an immobile one. The martial artist stands ready to grasp her foe as he approaches, rather than pursuing him. Until the martial artist\u2019s next action, if an enemy moves within close range, the martial artist may perform a reflexive grapple gambit. If she is armed with a net, she may do so if an enemy moves within her weapon\u2019s maximum range. Additionally, she may perform a reflexive grapple if she opposes a disengage roll and wins. If armed with a net, characters within short range must roll to disengage from her. Once the martial artist has successfully won control of a clinch, the effects of this Charm end.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mastery:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> This Charm\u2019s type is Reflexive, and may be activated in response to an enemy moving into range or attempting to disengage.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Silent Reef Form</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 8m; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 4, Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Simple, Decisive-Only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Form</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Permanent</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Entangled Krait Courtship, Polyp Proximity Strike</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The reef thrives on a thousand entangled lives, yet hardly makes a sound. The martial artist lowers the difficulty of disarm and grapple gambits by 1. While grappling or being grappled, she does not suffer the usual -2 Defense penalty. She restrains her victims with a powerful stranglehold, preventing them from speaking or breathing until her next turn. If she performs enough consecutive restraining actions to cause her foe to perish from lack of air, typically (their Stamina x2) rounds (</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Exalted</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">, pg. 232), they are instead incapacitated but alive. Once her enemy is incapacitated in this way, she must release him, leaving him unconscious but once again able able to breath.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Special activation rules: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">When the stylist initiates a grapple and wins the control roll, she may expend two rounds of control to reflexively enter this form.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Coral Body Mediation</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 4m; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 4, Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Dual, Mastery</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Silent Reef Form</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The martial artist tangles her own essence around herself, twisting and hardening her flesh against an attack. She gains +(higher of Essence or 3) Soak against </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">withering </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">attacks and (higher of Essence or 3) Hardness against </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">decisive </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">attacks. If she has not taken a movement action this round, she adds +2 to either her Soak or her Hardness. Against an opponent who controls a grapple against her or attacking barehanded, she also inflicts 1 level of </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">decisive </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">lethal damage, ignoring Hardness. So long as she has not performed a movement action since last activating this Charm, each subsequent activation reduces its cost by a cumulative 1 mote, to a minimum of 1 mote. Moving as part of a dragging action does not interfere with this Charm\u2019s effects.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mastery:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> If the martial artist has not performed a movement action, except as part of a dragging action, since her last activation of this Charm, its cost is reduced to 0 motes.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Hull-Breaching Atemi</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 6m, 3i; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 5, Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Mastery, Terrestrial, Withering-Only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Coral Body Meditation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">For every ship sunk by acts of war, two more have had their hulls torn asunder by the grasping reef. The martial artist performs a restraining action against a grappled enemy, reducing his Soak by -(higher of Essence or 3) until her next action. She may expend any number of rounds of control, with each round reducing the target\u2019s Soak by an additional -1. The martial artist also gains any initiative her opponent loses to </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">withering</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> attacks while under the influence of this Charm. If he crashes, the martial artist counts as the character responsible for crashing him for the purposes of future Initiative Shifts. On her next turn, the martial artist immediately releases her opponent. This charm can only be used once per scene, unless reset by crashing a grappled opponent. Even after resetting, this Charm cannot be used against the same enemy more than once in a scene.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mastery: </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">The stylist does not need to release her opponent on her next action.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Terrestrial:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> The Terrestrial cannot expend more than 5 rounds with this Charm.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Reef Captures Frigate</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 4m, 2i; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 5, Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Reflexive</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Counterattack, Decisive-Only, Terrestrial</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Coral Body Meditation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">When a vessel skirts to close to the reef, it should count itself lucky to only run aground. Against an attack made from close range, the martial artist gains +1 Parry. If the attack misses, she may counter attack with either a grapple gambit or a disarm gambit, adding her Parry as bonus dice to the attack roll. On a successful disarm gambit, she may keep hold of the weapon and use it as though it were compatible with this style until it leaves her hand.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Terrestrial:</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> This Charm counts as the Terrestrial\u2019s action for the turn and cannot be used if she has already acted.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Anemone Makes a Friend</span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: 8m, 4i, 1wp; </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mins</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Martial Arts 5, Essence 3</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Type</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Simple</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Keywords</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Decisive-Only</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Prerequisite Charms</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Hull-Breaching Atemi, Reef Captures Frigate</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Mastering the Silent Reef, the martial artist reexamines its earlier lessons and learns to restrain her foe with merely a touch. She makes a </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">decisive</span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> attack that exposes her victim to the Silent Reef Toxin. This poison has Damage 6i/turn (bashing in crash), duration (attack\u2019s threshold successes) rounds. Its penalty prevents its victim from speaking or breathing, potentially causing him to pass out if deprived of air long enough. In such cases, the victim is merely incapacitated rather than killed as with Silent Reef Form and beings breathing normally once unconscious. However, so long as the victim does not move away from the martial artist, the poison\u2019s onset is delayed. Once it has begun, it can be suspended again by moving back into close range. If the martial artist takes a move action away from her victim, the poison does not activate. The difficulty to diagnose the Silent Reef Toxin is +3 while active or +5 otherwise. After a day, the poison leaves his system if the victim has not yet triggered it.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2118,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","user":"Reminiscent Oasis","date":". 01-08-2020, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T02:31:52-08:00","id":1359867,"title":"","content":"This is cool, I've already noticed there's an interesting synergy between the form charm and the pinnacle.<br /> <br /> Ordinarily, Ex3 combats will end well before Silent Reef Form can make anyone suffocate <b>but </b>poison that deals initiative damage is a useful meta way to extend a fight. Someone who might launch their doom combo or surrender might hold off in favour of keeping moving so the poison keeps burns through initiative rather than vital health levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T05:35:11-08:00","id":1359883,"title":"","content":"Happy to hear you found this interesting. <br /> <br /> In the 2e version, the Form Charm also had a weaker variant of the poison tied to it. This time around, I made it a more mundane choke hold for the form and saved the supernatural poison for the pinnacle charm. <br /> <br /> As far as the duration of a fight is concerned, restraining an opponent prevents them from acting at all, so you don't have to worry about them building up their initiative for any big attacks too much. With Entangled Krait Courtship, you're minimizing (or negating) the number of rounds of control you have to sacrifice to maintain the restraint, so that helps extend things too. If he's got buddies trying to free him, then you've got The Clownfish Smiles to use him as a human shield against their attacks. Though that still consumes rounds of control for being attacked - I didn't give the Silent Reef any means of negating that issue.<br /> <br /> I did realized after posting this that the reflexive activation of the form is significantly weaker than Mantis Form, so I may have to reconsider that. Mantis Form just needs to control a clinch, and doesn't need to sacrifice any rounds of control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T06:48:16-08:00","id":1359892,"title":"","content":"First off: very cool Martial Art, with a clear thematic feel. I wanted to actually read it from your description, and the Charms didn't disappoint. Your costs feel roughly correct, in general, although I'll have a look again to make direct comparisons.<br /> <br /> Specific thoughts:<br /> There are no effects that reduce the penalty to round of control for being attacked when grappling, that I could see. That's probably intentional, but I thought I'd note it.<br /> <br /> Entangled Krait Courtship is.... Possibly going to end up as either really boring or completely overpowered in practice. It's Mastery abilities allows a Master to indefinitely restrain a target, which is boring for both participants. It also combines with the above problem to make it not a brilliant strategy if the victim has friends, but combines with the Form Charm to make it an unstoppable single-hit power if the target is weak to strangulation.<br /> <br /> Polyp Proximity Strike would probably benefit from having a clearly-stated duration, and the &quot;when used, stops working&quot; line, just for clarity. it's a cool ability, and looks like it would be fun to use. <br /> <br /> Coral Body Meditation is a brilliant ability, it's a charm I would really enjoy using, but I think it's another Charm that needs some tightening. It can be used &quot;reflexively&quot; and inflicts 1L against someone controlling a grapple against the practitioner. As written, I can't see why they can't just re-use it; it should probably say that it inflicts the damage after the attack.<br /> In terms of costing, 4m is a good price for 3-5 soak, and 4m for a turn of 5-7 soak at mastery is very attractive. I might bump the price a little, but it's probably fine as-is.<br /> <br /> Hull-Breaching Atemi kind of confuses me. It reduces an opponent's soak, potentially duplicates initiative gain, and the martial artist can't actually capitalize on the penalised soak because it wears off on their next action. It also had the withering-only tag on a restraining action. Is it supposed to be a savaging attack, so the martial artist definitely gets a benefit? Could it reduce soak to a negative value?. I'd say it's potentially a little weak, potential initiative duplication aside, as 6m for +3-5 damage is probably a better Charm for earlier in the tree.<br /> <br /> Having gone through this again, I realise that this style really benefits from being Strong and Dexteritous. Is that the archetype you have in mind for people who use this martial art?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12692-whybover","name":"Whybover","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-09T07:40:51-08:00","id":1359898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Whybover</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1359737-silent-reef-style-wip?p=1359892#post1359892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off: very cool Martial Art, with a clear thematic feel. I wanted to actually read it from your description, and the Charms didn't disappoint. Your costs feel roughly correct, in general, although I'll have a look again to make direct comparisons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you enjoyed the themes and snippet of lore there. The 2e version had more lore attached to it, but I'm still working on revamping that now that mortals can't practice martial arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Specific thoughts:<br /> There are no effects that reduce the penalty to round of control for being attacked when grappling, that I could see. That's probably intentional, but I thought I'd note it. </div> </div> </div>That is intentional. The style is good at effectively removing an opponent from the battle by restraining them, but falters if they have friends to liberate them from your grasp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Entangled Krait Courtship is.... Possibly going to end up as either really boring or completely overpowered in practice. It's Mastery abilities allows a Master to indefinitely restrain a target, which is boring for both participants. It also combines with the above problem to make it not a brilliant strategy if the victim has friends, but combines with the Form Charm to make it an unstoppable single-hit power if the target is weak to strangulation. </div> </div> </div>Just for clarity, when you say that the Mastery ability allows for indefinite restraining actions, you don't literally mean indefinite, right? This may be a case of me not fully understanding the rules here. As intended, this Charm is primarily to extend the length up the clinch up to its maximum duration as determined by your control roll for a Master, rather than 3 for non-Masters and 2 for everyone else (if my math is right). My understanding is that normally, when you perform a restraining action, that knocks off 2 rounds of control from its maximum duration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Polyp Proximity Strike would probably benefit from having a clearly-stated duration, and the &quot;when used, stops working&quot; line, just for clarity. it's a cool ability, and looks like it would be fun to use. </div> </div> </div>I'll see what I can do to clean that one up. It went through a couple recent revisions that I think may have muddied the waters a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Coral Body Meditation is a brilliant ability, it's a charm I would really enjoy using, but I think it's another Charm that needs some tightening. It can be used &quot;reflexively&quot; and inflicts 1L against someone controlling a grapple against the practitioner. As written, I can't see why they can't just re-use it; it should probably say that it inflicts the damage after the attack.<br /> In terms of costing, 4m is a good price for 3-5 soak, and 4m for a turn of 5-7 soak at mastery is very attractive. I might bump the price a little, but it's probably fine as-is. </div> </div> </div>Good point about re-application of damage. I'll include a restriction on that. I may also revert back to an earlier idea for the Mastery effect, which was to immediately reduce the re-application cost to 1m instead of 0m.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hull-Breaching Atemi kind of confuses me. It reduces an opponent's soak, potentially duplicates initiative gain, and the martial artist can't actually capitalize on the penalised soak because it wears off on their next action. It also had the withering-only tag on a restraining action. Is it supposed to be a savaging attack, so the martial artist definitely gets a benefit? Could it reduce soak to a negative value?. I'd say it's potentially a little weak, potential initiative duplication aside, as 6m for +3-5 damage is probably a better Charm for earlier in the tree. </div> </div> </div>The intent of this Charm is to be the inverse of the &quot;What if they have friends?&quot; problem you mentioned earlier. This is for the &quot;What if I have friends&quot; scenario. The martial artist is making her opponent vulnerable to any number of withering attacks from her allies, and benefits from the withering damage their attacks do as well. I can reword this one to make that intent more explicit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having gone through this again, I realise that this style really benefits from being Strong and Dexteritous. Is that the archetype you have in mind for people who use this martial art? </div> </div> </div>It's not opposed to my vision of a Silent Reef stylist, though now that you mention it, perhaps an emphasis on Strength isn't quite in line for them. I'm tempted to perhaps allow them to make a control roll with Dexterity if they use a net, but I don't want to make them too over-reliant on their weaponry.<br /> <br /> Thanks for taking the time to read through the style and comment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}